    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\">Hi Chris,<div><br></div><div>This is exactly what I was looking for. It is also much simpler than the path I was heading down.</div><div><br></div><div>Thank you,</div><div>Clayton <br><div><br><blockquote type=\"cite\"></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>On Apr 27, 2020, at 1:38 PM, Chris Sutherland &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">chris...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none\"><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Garamond,serif\">Hi Clayton,<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Garamond,serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Garamond,serif\">We did some of ‘structured pooling’ in our<span> </span><a href=\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-018-26847-x\" style=\"color:purple;text-decoration:underline\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-018-26847-x&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792492117848000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0Eonf0LeuQojjzHgYDB_lL\">mink paper</a><span> </span>and our<span> </span><a href=\"https://esj-journals.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1002/1438-390X.12045\" style=\"color:purple;text-decoration:underline\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://esj-journals.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1002/1438-390X.12045&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792492117848000&amp;usg=AOvVaw092BHuq8gvLpRSFm_Itf9V\">cheetah paper</a>. If I understand correctly, I think the following fabricated example is one approach.<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Garamond,serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Garamond,serif\">Let’s say we have 6 session, 3 in protected areas, 3 outside. The inference objective is to test whether density, sigma, or detection vary by protection status. So, without any covariates, we can easily estimate constant parameters (no variation, D~1) or, using the built in model ‘~Session’, we can estimate session-specific parameters. NB: this works for p0, Sig, and D. But, we can also so a lot more through creative covariate generation. Here is a way to add covariates to pool the protected and not protected sessions (‘Prot’ ‘uProt’, respectively).<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Garamond,serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><b><u><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Garamond,serif\">Density:<u></u><u></u></span></u></b></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Garamond,serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.5in;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:rgb(56,87,35)\">#6 sessions: 1-3 are Prot, 4-6 are uProt<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.5in;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:rgb(56,87,35)\"># ssDF is the ssDF object<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.5in;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:rgb(56,87,35)\"><u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.5in;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:rgb(56,87,35)\">prot &lt;- rep(c(‘Prot’,’uProt’),each=3)<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.5in;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:rgb(56,87,35)\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.5in;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:rgb(56,87,35)\">for(i in 1:6){<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.5in;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:rgb(56,87,35)\">  ssDF[[i]]$prot &lt;- factor(prot[i],levels= c(‘Prot’,’uProt’))<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.5in;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:rgb(56,87,35)\">}<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:rgb(56,87,35)\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;text-indent:0.5in\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Garamond,serif\">Now you can specify ~prot in the density model and estimate an intercept (Prot) and the coefficient (contract) for not protected. Likewise, you could add continuous variable to estimate effects (latitude for example).<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Garamond,serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Garamond,serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><b><u><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Garamond,serif\">Sigma:<u></u><u></u></span></u></b></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Garamond,serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.5in;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:rgb(56,87,35)\">#6 sessions: 1-3 are Prot, 4-6 are uProt<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.5in;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:rgb(56,87,35)\"># scrFrame is the scrFrame object<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.5in;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:rgb(56,87,35)\"># sigCovs is a dataframe with nSession rows, and nCovaraite columns.<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.5in;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:rgb(56,87,35)\"># i.e., sigCovs is like a session covariate data frame<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.5in;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:rgb(56,87,35)\"><u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.5in;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:rgb(56,87,35)\">scrFrame$sigCovs$prot &lt;- factor(rep(c(‘Prot’,’uProt’),each=3)) #adding the new covariate here<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;text-indent:0.5in\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Garamond,serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;text-indent:0.5in\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Garamond,serif\">Now you can specify ~prot in the sigma model and estimate an intercept (Prot) and the coefficient (contract) for not protected. Likewise, you could add continuous variable to estimate effects (latitude for example).<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Garamond,serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Garamond,serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><b><u><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Garamond,serif\">Baseline encounter (p0/g0):<u></u><u></u></span></u></b></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Garamond,serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.5in;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Garamond,serif\">In this case, following the same idea, you can add covariates to the tdf (add a column called prot, giving all traps is a session the same value). Now you can specify ~prot in the detection model and estimate an intercept (Prot) and the coefficient (contract) for not protected. Likewise, you could add continuous variable to estimate effects (latitude for example).<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:rgb(56,87,35)\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:rgb(56,87,35)\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Garamond,serif\">Using this approach gives a huge amount of flexibility in terms of ‘structured pooling’ beyond the simple ‘all or session’ approach that the majority of applications default to.<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Garamond,serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Garamond,serif\">Hope this helps, but if I’m way off the mark, let me know and I can have another go.<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Garamond,serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Garamond,serif\">Chris<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:rgb(56,87,35)\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Garamond,serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div><div><div style=\"border-style:solid none none;border-top-width:1pt;border-top-color:rgb(225,225,225);padding:3pt 0in 0in\"><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">From:</span></b><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span> </span><a href style=\"color:purple;text-decoration:underline\" data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">oscr_p...@googlegroups.com</a><span> </span>[<a href style=\"color:purple;text-decoration:underline\" data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mailto:oscr_p...@googlegroups.com</a>]<span> </span><b>On Behalf Of<span> </span></b>Clayton Lamb<br><b>Sent:</b><span> </span>Friday, April 24, 2020 11:49 AM<br><b>To:</b><span> </span><a href style=\"color:purple;text-decoration:underline\" data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">oscr_p...@googlegroups.com</a><br><b>Subject:</b><span> </span>[oscr] Pooling sessions<u></u><u></u></span></div></div></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><u></u> <u></u></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Hello,<u></u><u></u></div><div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><u></u> <u></u></div></div><div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">I have a large multi-session dataset (see screenshot) where I want to calculate sigma and dectection by session. Some sessions were quite sparsely sampled, and in that case I’d like to be able to pool these to share estimates. <u></u><u></u></div></div><div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><u></u> <u></u></div></div><div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">There are 42 sessions, and a few of them I would like to pool. For example 29:33 were all in the same place, just in different years, and sampling was low intensity (thus so were recaptures). I would like to pool these together and only estimate a single detection and sigma value across these, while estimating independent estimates across the other sessions. <u></u><u></u></div></div><div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><u></u> <u></u></div></div><div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">I feel like this must be easy, but I went down a rabbit hole of complex coding and decided to step back and ask the experts!<u></u><u></u></div></div><div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><u></u> <u></u></div></div><div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Cheers,<u></u><u></u></div></div></div></div></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
